  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: οἱ τυφλοί → *the blind men* is redivided under rule 102. The article takes the discontinuous *the … men* headed on *men*, and the adjective keeps a bare *blind*; the accepted reading applied rule 17's generic-noun clause, which rule 102 scopes in terms to anarthrous Greek and records JAS.1.11 as having corrected.",
    "The anarthrous `δύο τυφλοί` of the neighbouring verse is the contrast and is untouched: with no article to take the supplied nominal, the head stays on the adjective."
